## Summary

**What was failing:** The option parsing logic didn't handle the `-i` flag correctly. When an option started with `-` but wasn't `--with-filename`, `--no-filename`, `--recursive`, `--ignore-case`, or `--`, it checked if the second character was `'r'` first, then if it was `'H'` or `'h'`. The `-i` flag didn't match either condition, causing it to fall through to the usage error.

**What I changed:** Modified line 348 to also check for `argv[arg_idx][1] == 'i'` in addition to `'H'` and `'h'`, so that single-character options like `-i` are properly parsed by the combined short options handler.

**Build command:** `mkdir -p build && cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -pedantic -O2 src/new_grep/new_grep.c -o build/new_grep`

**Expected results:** All 113 tests now pass (previously 90/113 passed, 23 failing).
